{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone","id":703882,"title":"Are Kin mages overdone?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-16T16:06:06-07:00","id":703882,"title":"Are Kin mages overdone?","content":"the &quot;Kinfolk mage&quot; Is almost an unofficial sept position, in a lot of VTT Games I've seen any ideas why, is it just pigeon holing an idea into the game to broaden the player apeal or is it something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T16:10:43-07:00","id":703922,"title":"","content":"Snowflakes being snowflakes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T17:31:06-07:00","id":704054,"title":"","content":"Mages are really good at solving out of context problems or well generally being an out of context problem for most Garou antagonists. Garou are really good at filling in the weakness of mages being a lack of preparedness. People notice the ooc synergy and come up with reasons ot make it work IC. the Kin mage is probably the second laziest version the laziest of course being Dreamspeaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T19:38:21-07:00","id":704179,"title":"","content":"Since all the different splats have the merit Supernatural Companion, then it's part of they way the world is envisioned. Having the companion as a PC is a natural outgrowth of it. There is nothing snow flakey about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T21:28:16-07:00","id":704263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=704179#post704179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since all the different splats have the merit Supernatural Companion, then it's part of they way the world is envisioned. Having the companion as a PC is a natural outgrowth of it. There is nothing snow flakey about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no &quot;the&quot; world here, particularly when it comes to Werewolf and Mage. Supernatural Companion is more or less a freebie point tax for guaranteed crossover, and the ST is free to axe it if it doesn't fit the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T21:55:18-07:00","id":704275,"title":"","content":"Well, in my experience ever since the first game came out (VtM), most STs have used all the books for their games. If a ST was running a WtA game, if a vampire was used in the story it used the VtM rules, and the ST worked out all the details for the character, usually making it as badass as possible. If it was a Garou showing up in a VtM game, then expect it to have a full range of gifts. Most of the STs would let a PC do or play what ever they wanted as long as everyone had fun. I've played Garou in a VtM game, a vampire in a HtR game, etc. Yes, the ST is encouraged to used what ever part of the system he likes or discard anything he doesn't like. An example I've noticed is that a lot of STs have continued to not include rules from newer editions of the rules that down power the abilities of the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T22:03:13-07:00","id":704279,"title":"","content":"Well, Werewolves (and other Shapeshifters) tend to be picky, and go for the 'best and the brightest'. Mages certainly qualify.<br /> <br /> I do see it making more \u200bsense for Tribes like the Uktena to promote mystical abilities amongst their Kin than to form Camp to study it themselves.<br /> <br /> I don't see Shapeshifters really differentiating between Sorcerer, Psychic, and Mage; but I do see them being very picky about Paradigm.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T03:08:00-07:00","id":704588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone#post703882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the &quot;Kinfolk mage&quot; Is almost an unofficial sept position, in a lot of VTT Games I've seen any ideas why, is it just pigeon holing an idea into the game to broaden the player apeal or is it something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of Mages having sept positions makes me cringe. Even the singular, kindly Mage that really loves the Garou, does what they tell him and isn't killed by them will be treated with distrust and paranoia by the society at large.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Dreamspeaker kinfolk is so overdone it hurts. Dreamspeakers are cheapened by always shoving Werewolf down their throat. I love Werewolf to bits, but come on! Let the guys be themselves!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T06:55:12-07:00","id":704882,"title":"","content":"I did note &quot;Unofficial sept position&quot; As in he may not hold a formal position but its &quot;Almost expected&quot; <br /> <br /> oh?<br /> <br /> Why Dreamspeakers, why not Verbena?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T07:01:57-07:00","id":704891,"title":"","content":"Erm. Most Garou would like Verbena even less then Dreamspeakers. Better yet Verbena don't like shifters. Verbena paradigm is not very similar to what the Garou have to say about how reality works, and they will take offense. And Vice Versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T07:05:08-07:00","id":704894,"title":"","content":"Because the Dreamspeakers are the default &quot;spirit talkers&quot;. The Verbena focus more on the living material world while the Dreamspeakers focus on the ephemeral world more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T08:33:49-07:00","id":705154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=704275#post704275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in my experience ever since the first game came out (VtM), most STs have used all the books for their games.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't just quick reference guides for antagonists. They have their own styles, which are cramped severely by even the next most sympathetic game. Werewolf and Hunter have a fair bit in common on the street level, but they both make assumptions about how things work that are, from the perspective of the other game, really weird. Hunters can't even see into the Penumbra unless something is directly affecting the physical world right at that moment, or trying to build a bridge between the two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a ST was running a WtA game, if a vampire was used in the story it used the VtM rules, and the ST worked out all the details for the character, usually making it as badass as possible. If it was a Garou showing up in a VtM game, then expect it to have a full range of gifts. Most of the STs would let a PC do or play what ever they wanted as long as everyone had fun. I've played Garou in a VtM game, a vampire in a HtR game, etc. Yes, the ST is encouraged to used what ever part of the system he likes or discard anything he doesn't like. An example I've noticed is that a lot of STs have continued to not include rules from newer editions of the rules that down power the abilities of the characters. </div> </div> </div>The only ones who got a power-down in any significant form were the vampires, so that's something I'd avoid, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T11:06:29-07:00","id":705458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=704588#post704588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea of Mages having sept positions makes me cringe. Even the singular, kindly Mage that really loves the Garou, does what they tell him and isn't killed by them will be treated with distrust and paranoia by the society at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair garou society sort of sucks. I am pretty sure all the VTT septs with mage friends are also basically Psuedo Ahdi/Emerald Courts. Emerald Court actually would make sense. They have Ambassadors even from the Kumo","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T11:23:29-07:00","id":705507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705458#post705458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair garou society sort of sucks. I am pretty sure all the VTT septs with mage friends are also basically Psuedo Ahdi/Emerald Courts. Emerald Court actually would make sense. They have Ambassadors even from the Kumo</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Not from Kumo. Kumo are killed on sight.<br /> <br /> Garou Society does not suck. It's quite specific and it's pat of what makes them what they are. It's an old traditionalist culture with all the pluses and minuses that entails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T11:41:59-07:00","id":705561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705507#post705507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Not from Kumo. Kumo are killed on sight.<br /> <br /> Garou Society does not suck. It's quite specific and it's pat of what makes them what they are. It's an old traditionalist culture with all the pluses and minuses that entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read over the Kumo write up on 274 new CB book. That is not killed on Sight.<br /> <br /> No, Garou society Does suck. Not in the &quot;hey we can't have mages&quot; sense in that the Garou nation is incapable of having proper alliances with their fellow changing Breeds. But they can't because they are so full of themselves. The Ahdi was formed in less than a Decade. The Garou have never tried to fix the bridges they burned and apparently burned PROUDLY with the various wars of Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T12:01:11-07:00","id":705600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705561#post705561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read over the Kumo write up on 274 new CB book. That is not killed on Sight.<br /> <br /> No, Garou society Does suck. Not in the &amp;quot;hey we can't have mages&amp;quot; sense in that the Garou nation is incapable of having proper alliances with their fellow changing Breeds. But they can't because they are so full of themselves. The Ahdi was formed in less than a Decade. The Garou have never tried to fix the bridges they burned and apparently burned PROUDLY with the various wars of Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boo Hoo, the fuzzy wuzzys can't be super friends. Garou culture is based on survival of the fittest and might makes right. I'm pretty sure the only reason white wolf made the beast courts was to cater to the &quot;we are all friends&quot; crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T12:45:45-07:00","id":705636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705561#post705561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read over the Kumo write up on 274 new CB book. That is not killed on Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wtf. That's... new. And a 360 turn from what it used to be. Did they actually give any wider context in the book?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705561#post705561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Garou society Does suck. Not in the &quot;hey we can't have mages&quot; sense in that the Garou nation is incapable of having proper alliances with their fellow changing Breeds. But they can't because they are so full of themselves. The Ahdi was formed in less than a Decade. The Garou have never tried to fix the bridges they burned and apparently burned PROUDLY with the various wars of Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can have alliances with other Breeds. The Corax have been working fine. Nuwisha have been working with the Garou whether they like them or not. In the Amazon Gogol Fangs First has made amazing inroads with the local shifters. The Hengeyokai never had problems and not only did Blacktooth unite the shifters before the Ahadi, but now even after him there is a union of African shifters.<br /> <br /> Garou's fault is being prideful assholes who have a hard time apologising. You honestly don't know people like that? They are not exactly proud of what they did, and if handled correctly they will quite easily start working with others.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean they need a group of rogue reality breakers that seek to eat their resources and don't give a damn about their war to be &quot;better&quot;. They need to owe up to their mistakes and do what is right. And that's the job of the players.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T13:16:11-07:00","id":705644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705561#post705561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that the Garou nation is incapable of having proper alliances with their fellow changing Breeds. But they can't because they are so full of themselves. The Ahdi was formed in less than a Decade. The Garou have never tried to fix the bridges they burned and apparently burned PROUDLY with the various wars of Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wars of Rage were huge mistakes, but all wars are fraught with tragedy and misundertstandings. The First War of Rage is in the dim past, and though that is a big deal to the Mokole, most Garou have no knowledge or responsibility for what happened. Modern werewolves have almost nothing in common with their ancient ancestors anyway; for them it makes about as much sense as modern Mongolians having to acknowledge and apologize for what Ghengis Khan's hordes did to Europe and Asia.<br /> <br /> The War of Tears was not done with pride; it was a plot of the Black Spiral Dancers, and the Garou are trying to make amends and redeem Bat for what happened to the Camazotz. Even the Pure Ones, who the Fianna, Get and others fought tooth and nail just a century ago, are now allies. Seems like the Garou got over the 2nd War of Rage pretty quick.<br /> <br /> You say the Garou and their Nation are all dicks, but you seem to be under the impression that werewolves are some monolithic group that just runs around killing each other and the Fera. This seems like a knee-jerk and shallow interpretation of the setting, at best.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T16:11:19-07:00","id":705833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705600#post705600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Boo Hoo, the fuzzy wuzzys can't be super friends. Garou culture is based on survival of the fittest and might makes right. I'm pretty sure the only reason white wolf made the beast courts was to cater to the &quot;we are all friends&quot; crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> BOOHOO Why listen to Gaia when you can do it all yourself? That's the failure of Garou in a nutshell. There's more to long term survival than being good at punching. That's why the Garou are losing the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705644#post705644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Wars of Rage were huge mistakes, but all wars are fraught with tragedy and misundertstandings. The First War of Rage is in the dim past, and though that is a big deal to the Mokole, most Garou have no knowledge or responsibility for what happened. Modern werewolves have almost nothing in common with their ancient ancestors anyway; for them it makes about as much sense as modern Mongolians having to acknowledge and apologize for what Ghengis Khan's hordes did to Europe and Asia.<br /> <br /> The War of Tears was not done with pride; it was a plot of the Black Spiral Dancers, and the Garou are trying to make amends and redeem Bat for what happened to the Camazotz. Even the Pure Ones, who the Fianna, Get and others fought tooth and nail just a century ago, are now allies. Seems like the Garou got over the 2nd War of Rage pretty quick.<br /> <br /> You say the Garou and their Nation are all dicks, but you seem to be under the impression that werewolves are some monolithic group that just runs around killing each other and the Fera. This seems like a knee-jerk and shallow interpretation of the setting, at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say Garou are all dicks. I said the Garou Nation sucks. Its objectively not as good at doing what Gaia wants than a multi breed alliances would be. The Garou nation gives Garou the support to stand appart from others, It suggests that they stand apart from others. It makes standing apart from others tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:00:07-07:00","id":705890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705833#post705833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> BOOHOO Why listen to Gaia when you can do it all yourself? That's the failure of Garou in a nutshell. There's more to long term survival than being good at punching. That's why the Garou are losing the Apocalypse.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would the setting be as fun if they were winning? If it was all *Meanwhile at the Hall of Gaia*?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:23:43-07:00","id":705902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705890#post705890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would the setting be as fun if they were winning? If it was all *Meanwhile at the Hall of Gaia*?</div> </div> </div> </div> You mean a setting where the Tribes (or at least, a few of them) have set up fiefdoms and technology is highly controlled, or highly underground?<br /> <br /> Sounds like a blast, actually.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:26:43-07:00","id":705906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705902#post705902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> You mean a setting where the Tribes (or at least, a few of them) have set up fiefdoms and technology is highly controlled, or highly underground?<br /> <br /> Sounds like a blast, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that's the opposite of my superfriends analogy however it does sound pretty awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:31:20-07:00","id":705919,"title":"","content":"Children of Gaia even shadow lords ARE trying to fix those bridges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T17:54:08-07:00","id":705945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705906#post705906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually that's the opposite of my superfriends analogy however it does sound pretty awesome</div> </div> </div> </div> That's because the 'Superfriends' analogy is so badly overdone at this point, it holds no weight. It's no more likely to happen in a game with Fera or a game with a Vampire, a Mage, and a Werewolf than it is to happen in a game with a 5 Garou.<br /> <br /> And it isn't like there wasn't a precedent since first edition. The war against Set started the idea that the Garou (and others) could get it together\u200b if the threat was big enough, and in modern nights, the threats just seem to be getting worse and worse. (And more numerous.)<br /> <br /> (Of course, I think it's a shame that the CoG seem to be nowhere to be found in any of the more recent developments.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T19:49:35-07:00","id":706107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=705890#post705890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would the setting be as fun if they were winning? If it was all *Meanwhile at the Hall of Gaia*?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally it would be nice if the game didnt quite drive the point of &quot;we losing the war, we losing the war, we losing the war. The apocalypse is coming no matter what you do and garous are not fit to face it&quot; home every chance it gets. Which makes many ST to drop cosmic anvils when one starts try something different than &quot;last stand&quot;. Of course thats more fault of the said DMs than the game but still.<br /> <br /> I havent encountered that much games with kinfolk mages, maybe 1 but i dont really mind. I mean i kinda like the fact is one of those relations between supernatural that doesnt boil down to the boring &quot;stay out of/kill on sight&quot; as many others in WoD.<br /> <br /> Dont get me wrong, i personally dont like crossovers but thats because of the umbalanced mechanics but i appreciate the option being open.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T00:16:31-07:00","id":706436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=706107#post706107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally it would be nice if the game didnt quite drive the point of &quot;we losing the war, we losing the war, we losing the war. The apocalypse is coming no matter what you do and garous are not fit to face it&quot; home every chance it gets. Which makes many ST to drop cosmic anvils when one starts try something different than &quot;last stand&quot;. Of course thats more fault of the said DMs than the game but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, but I would say those folks lost sight of the reason we are playing WtA. The Dying Earth trope can be played straight but that does not mean everything is hopeless and the PC's pack is doomed. 'We are losing' is only half of the shtick. The other half of that is 'so what are you gonna do about it, punk?' And your answer as players (and a storyteller!) should be something awesome. Smacking the Wyrm around and turning Malfeas into a second Summer Country might be little much, but the games don't have to culminate in dreary suicide attacks, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T04:18:33-07:00","id":706616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/703882-are-kin-mages-overdone?p=706436#post706436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair point, but I would say those folks lost sight of the reason we are playing WtA. The Dying Earth trope can be played straight but that does not mean everything is hopeless and the PC's pack is doomed. 'We are losing' is only half of the shtick. The other half of that is 'so what are you gonna do about it, punk?' And your answer as players (and a storyteller!) should be something awesome. Smacking the Wyrm around and turning Malfeas into a second Summer Country might be little much, but the games don't have to culminate in dreary suicide attacks, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here, have a cookie. Heck, have the whole box!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T17:06:53-07:00","id":707730,"title":"","content":"Answer to the OP. Yes. Yes they are. All the snowflakes I see from this would equal to one of the blizzards we get here in Minnesota.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T18:40:10-07:00","id":707907,"title":"","content":"I enjoy blizzards.","signature":"<hr class